mmunohistochemical and two-parameter flow cytometric studies of DNA topoisomerase II alpha in human epithelial ovarian carcinoma and germ cell tumor</article-title><source>Mod Pathol</source><year>1998</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>186</fpage><lpage>193</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9504690</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holden</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>DNA topoisomeraseII a as a proliferation marker in endocrine and other neoplasms</article-title><source>Endocr Pathol</source><year>1999</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>97</fpage><lpage>102</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF02739821</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holden</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Perkins</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Snow</surname><given-names>GW</given-names></name><name><surname>Hjeldsberg</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Immunohistochemica staining for DNA topoisomerase II in non-Hodgkin's lymphomas</article-title><source>Am J Clin Pathol</source><year>1995</year><volume>104</volume><fpage>54</fpage><lpage>59</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7611182</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mao</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Detection of Epstein-Barr virus (EBV) DNA by the polymerase chain reaction (PCR) in oral smears from healthy individuals and patients with oral squamous cell carcinoma</article-title><source>J Oral Pathol Med</source><year>1993</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>12</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8380451</pub-id><pub-id pub-i